**Coding summary — Stacey Donato / education-library-books**

Three passages, all one record group on `HB 1447 (2023)`, all `own-act`, `record`, `in-term` (2023 act; term began 2019):

| Snapshot | Role in the record | V4 shape |
|---|---|---|
| Bill details page | sponsor line (`actor_quote`) | `multi-subject` |
| Enrolled text PDF | the school library provision (`provision_quote`) | `direction-only` |
| Roll call 520 | her Yea + tally (`actor_quote`, `tally_quote`) | `multi-subject` |

**Chair: BLANK `direction-only`.** Two independent defects:

1. **Clause mismatch.** IC 20-26-5.5 creates a removal-*request* process open to parents, guardians, and community members, reviewed by "the governing body … at the next public meeting." That is review-gated, so it is not rung 4 (pull on challenge) and not rung 5 (remove on report); and the reviewer is the elected school board, not "a review committee of educators and parents," so rung 3 isn't matched either. It shows direction toward restriction without separating 3/4/5.
2. **Multi-subject instrument.** HB 1447 bundles Muncie school flexibility, third-party vendor surveys, political-activism neutrality, the library chapter, and criminal obscenity defenses. Under V4.1 a final-passage vote on it proves direction at most, and no statement of hers in the sources ties her vote to the library sections.

Tally 39–10 (10 of 49 voting Nay), so `near-unanimous` does not apply — the defect is subject-bundling, not margin.

I did not quote anything inside a `[deleted: …]` fence, per §5 of the amendment-markup rule; note that SECTION 6's narrowing of the harmful-to-minors defense sits in deleted markup, so it is not available as `provision_quote`.

`needs_source` flags three gaps: the as-introduced/as-sponsored version of HB 1447 (the details-page digest describes only the survey provisions, so the library chapter may have been added in conference — C37 matters here), her own words tying the vote to the library sections, and any single-subject Indiana library-materials bill with a Donato act.
